<Layout title={title} description={description}>
<section class="detail-hero">
    <div class="container">
        <a href="research.html" class="back-link">← Back to Research</a>
        <span class="eyebrow">OPTICAL WIRELESS COMMUNICATIONS · FPGA PROTOTYPING</span>
        <h1>128-QAM SC-FDM Optical Wireless System</h1>
        <p>Real-time digital signal processing, high-order constellation mapping, and hardware verification for high-speed optical communications.</p>
    </div>
</section>

<section class="section">
    <div class="container detail-layout">
        <article class="detail-content">
            <img class="project-image" src="assets/research-128qam-scfdm.jpg" alt="128-QAM SC-FDM Optical Wireless Communication System Constellation and FPGA Testbed">
            
            <h2>Project Overview</h2>
            <p>At BONLAB, we investigate the realization of Single-Carrier Frequency Division Multiplexing (SC-FDM) combined with high-order Quadrature Amplitude Modulation (128-QAM) for optical wireless links. SC-FDM provides lower Peak-to-Average Power Ratio (PAPR) compared to traditional OFDM, making it exceptionally well-suited for optical emitters with nonlinear transfer characteristics.</p>
            
            <p>Our team implements real-time baseband DSP blocks directly into FPGA hardware, validating theoretical error-vector magnitude (EVM) and bit error rate (BER) through physical optical channels.</p>

            <h2>Key Innovations & Technical Highlights</h2>
            <ul class="detail-list">
                <li><strong>High Spectral Efficiency:</strong> 128-QAM modulation constellation design providing dense information throughput.</li>
                <li><strong>Low PAPR Performance:</strong> SC-FDM discrete Fourier transform (DFT) precoding to prevent laser diode saturation.</li>
                <li><strong>FPGA Real-Time DSP:</strong> Pipelined digital filtering, equalization, and symbol synchronization implemented on programmable digital hardware.</li>
                <li><strong>Low Phase-Noise PLL:</strong> Customized phase-locked loop synchronization reducing phase jitter in optical carrier recovery.</li>
            </ul>

            <h2>Laboratory Verification & Testbeds</h2>
            <p>Experiments were conducted in the BONLAB facilities at RMUTI Khon Kaen Campus using high-bandwidth arbitrary waveform generators, mixed-signal oscilloscopes, semiconductor laser modules, and high-speed photodetectors.</p>

            <h2>Official Research Profile</h2>
            <p>For more research publications, datasets, and citation metrics, visit our official Scopus / ORCID profile.</p>
            <a class="text-link" href="https://orcid.org/0000-0002-8698-5407" target="_blank" rel="noopener">View Assoc. Prof. Dr. Kidsanapong Puntsri on ORCID →</a>
        </article>

